{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shores\nA land of wonder and enchantment that doth await thee\nThy travels shall begin in Tokyo's bustling streets\nWhere ancient temples meet modern skyscrapers' lofty seats\n\nDay the first thou shalt arrive in Tokyo's Narita gate\nAnd make thy way to thy lodging with haste and speed\nThe remainder of the day thou shalt spend in rest\nAnd prepare thyself for the wonders that tomorrow shall bring\n\nDay the second thou shalt rise with morning's early light\nAnd visit the famous Tsukiji Fish Market's bustling sight\nThou shalt behold the freshest seafood in all the land\nAnd sample some of the local delicacies with eager hand\n\nNext thou shalt make thy way to the Meiji Shrine's sacred ground\nA tranquil oasis in the midst of Tokyo's crowded round\nThou shalt pay thy respects to the deified spirits of old\nAnd learn of Japan's rich history and storied past\n\nDay the third thou shalt travel to Nikko's ancient town\nA UNESCO World Heritage Site of great renown\nThou shalt behold the Toshogu Shrine's ornate beauty and might\nAnd marvel at the craftsmanship of Japan's skilled artisans in sight\n\nDay the fourth thou shalt journey to Kyoto's cultural heart\nA city of temples and gardens that doth never depart\nThou shalt visit the Fushimi Inari Shrine's famous orange gates\nAnd hike the winding trails that lead to the mountain's sacred states\n\nDay the fifth thou shalt explore Kyoto's Nijo Castle's grounds\nA fortress of great beauty and historical renown\nThou shalt walk the castle's \"nightingale floors\" with stealthy tread\nAnd learn of the castle's secrets and hidden passages unsaid\n\nDay the sixth thou shalt travel to Hiroshima's somber shore\nA city of peace and remembrance that doth forever roar\nThou shalt visit the Hiroshima Peace Memorial Park's solemn grounds\nAnd pay thy respects